  "final_answer": "I have all the information needed. Let me confirm the details before providing the answer.\n\nThe page explicitly mentions \"应用的学习项目\" (Applied Learning Project) and describes \"Hands-on labs emphasize interactivity and graphic design\" which confirms the specialization includes projects.\n\n## Final Answer\n\n**Specialization Name:** Data Visualization\n\n**Institution:** Johns Hopkins University\n\n**Skills Developed:**\n- Data Visualization Software\n- Data Literacy\n- Spatial Data Analysis\n- Tableau Software\n- Graphic and Visual Design\n- Data Storytelling\n- Data Presentation\n- Computer Displays\n- Statistical Visualization\n\n**Project Inclusion:** Yes — The specialization includes applied learning projects. According to the page description, it \"combines theory and practice\" and includes \"hands-on labs [that] emphasize interactivity and graphic design to craft impactful, actionable visualizations.\" It also mentions \"借助实践项目精通一门科目或一个工具\" (master a subject or tool through hands-on projects).\n\n**Additional Details:**\n- Rating: 4.7 (12 reviews)\n- Level: Intermediate\n- Length: 3-6 months\n- Number of courses: 3 courses\n- Number of students: 2,526\n- Instructor: Jesus Caban\n\n**Course list:**\n1. Foundations of Data Visualization\n2. Advanced Techniques in Data Visualization\n3. Specialized Data Visualization Approaches\n\n**Summary:** The specialization is intended for post-graduate students seeking to develop advanced data visualization skills. It covers both foundational concepts (design principles, data representation) and specialized methods (network visualization, volume rendering, 3D exploration using tools like ParaView).",
